{"n": 601, "w": 1000, "h": 1309, "img": "601.webp", "text": "In case of more than one fault, this section is\nrepeated as often as the number of faults.\n\n32-52\n\nTROUBLESHOOTING A — Indicator Lamp On Continuously — (Cipro Diagnosis Unit)\n\nThe “airbag system” employs a fault detector and memory, even for briefly occurring faults. If the “airbag indicator lamp” does not go out after\nStarting, there could be one or more faults. A flashing code from the indicator lamp will help only personnel with qualified training in BMW service\nto pinpoint and eliminate the faults.\n\nThe flashing code can be called by performing the following procedures and as often as desired,\n\nA) Turn off the ignition,\n\n8) Connect airbag diagnosis plug 62 1 250 in the engine diagnosis socket (pins 1 and 6 are bridged), use adapter 62 1 140 if necessary.\nC) Turn the ignition lock to position 1.\n\nFlashing code will now run off and the number of flashes must be counted.\n\n3s\n\n3s\n\n3s\n\n3s\n\n3s\n\n3s\n\n3s\n3s\n\nBulb test\n\nFlashes 1 to 3 times depending on the number of faults\nDark\nStart for fault code\n\nDark\n\nFlashes 1 to 3 times — note number — for example\n= —\n\nFlashes 1 to 4 times — note number — for example — 3 — 4 — 2 — see fault code table\n\n~TLo_t\n\nDark\n\nFlashes 1 or 2 times ~ note number — for exam\nDark\n\n1 time for a brief fault (e.g. short interruption of plug contact)\n\nFlashes ¥ or 2 times — 2 times for parmanent fault\n\nDark\n\nBreak/start with more than 1 fault repeat\nLamp on continuously — end of check control", "words": [["In", 0.2745, 0.0172, 0.2845, 0.0268], ["case", 0.2745, 0.0304, 0.2825, 0.0507], ["of", 0.2745, 0.0542, 0.2851, 0.0638], ["more", 0.2739, 0.0679, 0.2818, 0.0922], ["than", 0.2739, 0.0952, 0.2845, 0.1155], ["one", 0.2739, 0.1185, 0.2812, 0.1358], ["fault,", 0.2719, 0.1393, 0.2845, 0.1641], ["this", 0.2732, 0.1677, 0.2838, 0.1849], ["section", 0.2732, 0.1879, 0.2818, 0.2214], ["is", 0.2732, 0.2249, 0.2812, 0.232], ["repeated", 0.